{#
  STATEMENT — Figma 6:25758. Copy from _data/statement.js.

  THE PAGE FRAME CONTINUES THROUGH THIS SECTION. 185:1994 carries left and
  right borders, so the 1272 column runs unbroken from the hero above into My
  Work below. They are pseudo-elements on the section rather than borders on
  the inner box, exactly as .hero, .about and .work draw theirs — see
  _statement.css for why.

  data-header-theme="light" because this is a white band: the header has to
  stay on its light palette while this is the section under it, the same as the
  hero above and About below.

  NO REVEAL-ON-SCROLL. None of the redesign sections animate in — reveal.js is
  a v2 leftover at the repo root that base.njk does not load — so this one does
  not either.

  ONE <p> PER AUTHORED LINE. The break between them is in the comp; the second
  line's wrap onto a third visual line is not (see statement.js).
#}

<section class="statement" data-header-theme="light">
  <div class="statement__inner">
    <div class="statement__text">
      {%- for line in statement.lines %}
        <p class="statement__line">{{ line }}</p>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
